ping\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/logs/combo_a251c730/20260502_192150/gen_21.log:5765:+#      and no-rotation stamping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/logs/combo_a251c730/20260502_192150/gen_21.log:5962:+def _stamp_entries(out: np.ndarray, entries: list[dict]) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/logs/combo_a251c730/20260502_192150/gen_21.log:5991:+    _stamp_entries(out, entries)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/logs/combo_a251c730/20260502_192150/gen_21.log:6044:+    - Clear the destination interior first, stamp markers in ascending anchor-color order, and let later stamps overwrite earlier ones where rotated footprints overlap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/logs/combo_a251c730/20260502_192150/gen_21.log:6046:+    Key insight: The marker color still selects the sprite, but the marker position controls orientation and the anchor-color ordering controls which rotated stamp stays visible in overlap zones.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/logs/combo_a251c730/20260502_192150/gen_21.log:6226:+    _stamp_entries(out, entries)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/logs/combo_a251c730/20260502_192150/gen_21.log:6466:+#      then stamp each matched sprite into the destination rectangle so the anchor pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/logs/combo_a251c730/20260502_192150/gen_21.log:6470:+#    - D10 adds a temporal control: stamps are no longer conceptually simultaneous.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/logs/combo_a251c730/20260502_192150/gen_21.log:6477:+#         rotated masks overlap, the color-8 stamp is applied second and covers the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/logs/combo_a251c730/20260502_192150/gen_21.log:6491:+#    - The original direct-stamp assumption breaks twice: rotation changes the anchor's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/logs/combo_a251c730/20260502_192150/gen_21.log:6492:+#      relative coordinates, and overlapping stamps make iteration order semantically\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/logs/combo_a251c730/20260502_192150/gen_21.log:6496:+#      The generator keeps 