{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n \\\"Key insight:.*marker|方向标记|direction marker|launcher\\\" /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code -g '*.py'\"","aggregated_output":"/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/a32d8b75.py:274:    Key insight: The marker pixel's position in a 3x3 grid jointly encodes vertical and horizontal anchor alignment (start/middle/end).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/7b3084d4.py:265:    Key insight: The lone marker pixel picks the anchor and fixes the output orientation — it must sit at the top-left corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/faa9f03d.py:51:    Key insight: The singleton markers identify which sparse stroke fragments belong together; after they are colored, the intended lines are the axis-aligned gaps between facing endpoints, with yellow controls flipping one arm to the marked side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/247ef758.py:45:    Key insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/e8686506.py:184:    Key insight: Left-right symmetry plus the no-same-color-touching constraint make the assembly unique; corner/edge markers anchor it when present.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/5545f144.py:206:    Key insight: The triangle's tip encodes facing direction, which sets marker-consumption priority.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/53fb4810.py:118:    Key insight: Each marker's attachment side determines its extension direction; the pattern repeats periodically, not as a single copy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/9385bd28.py:86:    Key insight: The L-shaped anchors sit on the marker diagonal; the fill goes on the opposite diagonal of the bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/13e47133.py:68:    Key insight: Each marker's depth from the boundary defines its position in the cyclic palette; the pattern then tiles inward automatically.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/7ed72f31.py:21:    Key insight: Red marker geometry (line vs single pixel) determines reflection type; isolated vs embedded red determines what gets reflected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/6e4f6532.py:40:    Key insight: Coupler count selects the docking target; marker color encodes which boundary stripe to face, fixing the unique orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2d0172a1/D2/2/code.py:334:    Key insight: Wobbly frame geometry is irrelevant, but blob area is now a meaningful parameter that controls the output marker shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/aa62e3f4.py:33:    Key insight: The colored interior marker supplies the paint color, while the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/981add89.py:27:    The top row is a set of vertical ray launchers; each ray toggles only cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:58:    - The maroon contact side is a launcher: it determines a unique outward ray for the whole object, and the edge of the grid determines the translation distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D2/1/code.py:16:      - green(3): a direction marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D2/1/code.py:46:    - To keep the cue visible and not overly free-form, the direction marker uses\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D2/1/code.py:80:      every sample: direction marker behind the parent-facing connector.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D2/1/code.py:85:    - Green is reserved exclusively for direction markers; the generator enforces\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D2/1/code.py:192:    Reassemble scattered sprites around the fixed yellow anchor by using both connector pixels and direction markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D2/1/code.py:335:PIECE_COLORS = [1, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9]  # green(3) is reserved for direction markers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/182e5d0f.py:102:    Key insight: The blac